[kuento@kuhub.cc.ukans.edu writes:]
[]    How many folks have had the problem where they get the prompt
[] "In your haste, you rip the scroll to pieces" when trying to use a
[] magic marker on a blank scroll? I've never even gotten to the point
[] where I'm asked what I want to write! I just don't understand what's
[] going wrong here, despite numerous permutations of attempts. So, what
[] *is* the big trick here?

it's a bug, IMO, some would consider it a feature.  the game is
being coy with you.  you know its a blank scroll, probably because
you just manufactured it or something, however until you identify it
as a blank scroll then the game doesn't understand that you know and
presumes that you are being hasty about writing scrolls.  the big
trick: read the blank scroll and it'll tell you: hah! that scroll
was blank (or something, like you didn't know).  now the game knows
that you know the scroll was blank and you can proceed to write
on it ...

